    a: "Companies buy other companies to grow faster, cut costs or gain capabilities they can't build quickly. A deal creates value for the buyer only if the target's standalone value plus synergies exceeds the price and costs. Bankers test deals with a merger model: combine both companies' earnings, adjust for how the deal is paid for and compare pro forma EPS with the buyer's own. Around it sit the purchase price allocation, the choice of cash or stock, the exchange ratio, tax structure and deal protections.",
