    q: "What's the difference between revenue and cost synergies, and why do buyers trust cost synergies more?",
    a: "Cost synergies are savings from combining: closing duplicate offices and plants, removing overlapping roles and buying at better prices. Revenue synergies are extra sales from cross-selling, wider distribution or pricing. Buyers trust cost synergies more because they control them; revenue synergies depend on customers and competitors, so investors give them little credit.",
