    q: "Walk me through a purchase price allocation.",
    a: "Start with the purchase equity value. Take the target's book equity and remove its existing goodwill, which doesn't carry over. Write identifiable assets up to fair value, usually PP&E and intangibles such as customer relationships and brands. In a stock deal, record a deferred tax liability on the write-ups, because the tax basis doesn't change. The price above the resulting identifiable net assets is goodwill.",
