    why: "Section 382 stops profitable companies from buying loss companies just to shelter their own income. The cap lets the NOLs shelter roughly what the target's own value would earn at a low, safe rate, so a small company with large NOLs gives a buyer little. The IRS publishes the rate monthly. The limit sits on top of the 80%-of-taxable-income cap for post-2017 losses, and any unused limit carries forward to later years. So buyers value acquired NOLs as the present value of tax actually saved.",
