    a: "A fixed ratio gives the target's holders a set number of acquirer shares, so the offer's dollar value moves with the acquirer's stock: they bear the price risk and ownership is locked. A fixed price gives them a set dollar value, so the acquirer issues more shares if its stock falls: its holders bear the risk and ownership floats.",
